WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.069
(fast drumming)

00:00:02.069 --> 00:00:06.890
(fast hard rock music)

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.460
- The world of sound that is created by

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.951
so many musicians is so strong
that you get goosebumps.

00:00:13.951 --> 00:00:16.041
You get slaps on your face

00:00:16.041 --> 00:00:17.880
and punched in the stomach.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.520
It's very, very intense and powerful.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.520
I'm not really able to translate it

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.783
into words; you just have to see it.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.970
My name is Fabio Zaffagnini,
and I'm the founder

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.250
of Rockin'1000 ...

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.217
The biggest rock band on earth.

00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:43.209
Rockin'1000 is a band
composed of thousands

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.190
and thousands of musicians coming from

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.450
all over the world.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.130
We organize massive events

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:51.373
where more than a thousand
musicians perform simultaneously.

00:00:52.226 --> 00:00:54.812
We have 400 guitars,

00:00:54.812 --> 00:00:58.905
250 drummers, 300 bassists,

00:00:58.905 --> 00:01:01.810
350 singers.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:04.680
We have musicians coming
from 30 different countries

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.513
in the world:

00:01:05.513 --> 00:01:07.690
from South Korea, from the United States,

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.816
from Canada, from Brazil, Russia, Iran.

00:01:10.816 --> 00:01:15.570
(rock music)

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:18.160
The logistic challenge is quite big.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.100
Hundreds and hundreds of people

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.409
build the stage, which is
as big as a football field.

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:25.731
We have hundreds of microphones,

00:01:25.731 --> 00:01:28.575
miles and miles of wires and cables.

00:01:28.575 --> 00:01:30.593
It's crazy.

00:01:30.593 --> 00:01:32.670
All the musicians have to prepare

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.850
from home, and once they come here,

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.300
they will have like
three days of rehearsals-

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.503
very intense days.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.530
They get to meet each other.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.586
They start playing and meld together

00:01:48.586 --> 00:01:50.283
and build the magic.

00:01:56.137 --> 00:02:00.784
The main message behind
Rockin'1000 is the spirit

00:02:00.784 --> 00:02:02.970
of togetherness.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:03.910
The idea that people

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.700
that generally play in their basement

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.150
or sing under the shower,

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.400
when they're all together,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.170
they can really make the difference

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:13.521
and it's a message that goes
far beyond music, I think.

00:02:13.521 --> 00:02:17.053
We make no difference of
the sexual orientation,

00:02:17.053 --> 00:02:19.854
political orientation,
religious orientation,

00:02:19.854 --> 00:02:23.190
rich or poor, professionals or newbies.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.900
We include everybody.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.140
They're all together
because of rock and roll.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:29.973
(hard rock music)

